1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,535
(This drama complied with production
guidelines for filming child actors,)

2
00:00:01,538 --> 00:00:02,949
(and some scenes used
generative AI technology.)

3
00:00:03,144 --> 00:00:04,549
(Episode 23)

4
00:00:04,552 --> 00:00:05,566
Go home today.

5
00:00:05,887 --> 00:00:08,105
Ji Hu seems to have a lot on his mind.

6
00:00:12,651 --> 00:00:13,742
This is so annoying.

7
00:00:13,744 --> 00:00:15,795
I spent all that money for this?

8
00:00:20,918 --> 00:00:21,951
I'll go.

9
00:00:31,518 --> 00:00:33,752
Hey, go after her.

10
00:00:34,080 --> 00:00:36,155
Go apologize and comfort her!

11
00:00:36,589 --> 00:00:37,589
Hurry!

12
00:00:38,431 --> 00:00:39,756
I have nothing to say to her.

13
00:00:40,157 --> 00:00:42,142
- What?
- I said I have nothing to say.

14
00:00:42,144 --> 00:00:43,151
Ji Hu.

15
00:00:48,268 --> 00:00:49,362
How could you?

16
00:00:50,558 --> 00:00:52,432
Why are you doing this?

17
00:00:53,425 --> 00:00:54,946
Do you know how much those paintings cost?

18
00:00:55,709 --> 00:00:58,138
And who do you think
I spent that money for?

19
00:00:58,745 --> 00:01:02,223
How could you treat me like this?

20
00:01:22,465 --> 00:01:24,502
Mom told me to run after you
and hold you back,

21
00:01:24,550 --> 00:01:26,858
and dad told me
to think about our relationship.

22
00:01:26,893 --> 00:01:27,903
Think about what?

23
00:01:28,531 --> 00:01:29,591
What is there to think about?

24
00:01:31,818 --> 00:01:32,945
Is there another woman?

25
00:01:33,685 --> 00:01:34,811
Is she richer than me?

26
00:01:34,813 --> 00:01:37,197
- More successful than my dad?
- Why me, then?

27
00:01:37,732 --> 00:01:38,771
Like you said,

28
00:01:39,459 --> 00:01:41,487
plenty of men would bow down
to someone like you.

29
00:01:41,948 --> 00:01:42,948
Why me?

30
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:46,058
- That's...
- Because I hid your study-abroad lie?

31
00:01:47,312 --> 00:01:49,220
Only you and my mom know.

32
00:01:50,205 --> 00:01:52,758
My mom told me
to treat you well no matter what.

33
00:01:52,852 --> 00:01:54,523
That doesn't matter to me.

34
00:01:54,525 --> 00:01:56,870
That's why I let it go.
You're all that matters to me!

35
00:02:00,012 --> 00:02:01,029
But now,

36
00:02:02,430 --> 00:02:03,494
my heart's wavering.

37
00:02:04,468 --> 00:02:05,691
It's wavering!

38
00:02:06,438 --> 00:02:09,231
Ji Hu, please don't do this.

39
00:02:09,671 --> 00:02:10,679
Today,

40
00:02:10,720 --> 00:02:12,346
while I was having
these paintings wrapped,

41
00:02:12,854 --> 00:02:13,879
I was so excited.

42
00:02:14,214 --> 00:02:16,084
Do you know how many things I imagined?

43
00:02:17,290 --> 00:02:18,500
Your face...

44
00:02:19,728 --> 00:02:20,903
Would you smile widely?

45
00:02:21,624 --> 00:02:22,851
Would you try to hide it?

46
00:02:22,951 --> 00:02:23,980
Then I thought,

47
00:02:24,588 --> 00:02:26,152
should I kiss you?

48
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:27,518
Or hug you?

49
00:02:31,925 --> 00:02:33,331
I feel so pathetic.

50
00:02:41,605 --> 00:02:43,623
Dad said he'd buy the painting.

51
00:02:44,816 --> 00:02:46,878
- Really?
- I refused.

52
00:02:48,358 --> 00:02:50,399
I said I'd accept this failure.

53
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:51,791
Ji Hu.

54
00:02:53,291 --> 00:02:55,245
It seems we really don't know each other.

55
00:02:57,678 --> 00:02:59,085
What are you trying to say?

56
00:03:00,638 --> 00:03:02,802
I want to find the person
I was when I loved you.

57
00:03:04,125 --> 00:03:05,348
What I felt,

58
00:03:05,875 --> 00:03:08,680
and why I chose you as my fiancée,

59
00:03:09,932 --> 00:03:11,045
I'll think it over again.

60
00:03:12,465 --> 00:03:14,172
I'll return the painting tomorrow.

61
00:03:14,729 --> 00:03:15,738
Just know that.

62
00:03:18,318 --> 00:03:19,335
Ji Hu...

63
00:03:21,043 --> 00:03:22,058
Ji Hu...

64
00:03:23,705 --> 00:03:25,552
Please don't think about it.

65
00:03:27,051 --> 00:03:28,748
Let's just be like we used to...

66
00:03:32,949 --> 00:03:33,965
I'll take you home.

67
00:03:37,245 --> 00:03:38,248
Okay?

68
00:03:39,275 --> 00:03:40,858
I'm not too young to go home by myself.

69
00:03:46,531 --> 00:03:48,324
(One week later)

70
00:03:49,032 --> 00:03:51,201
So far, everything is going very well.

71
00:03:51,482 --> 00:03:52,482
You want to see him, right?

72
00:03:55,465 --> 00:03:57,758
I don't know how this week passed.

73
00:03:58,452 --> 00:03:59,564
Every morning,

74
00:04:00,112 --> 00:04:02,701
I hoped O Reum would...

75
00:04:03,007 --> 00:04:04,238
make it through another day.

76
00:04:04,558 --> 00:04:06,091
I'm sure the whole family did.

77
00:04:06,672 --> 00:04:09,919
Now that the transplant is done,
we'll move him once it engrafts.

78
00:04:10,105 --> 00:04:11,137
You can see him then.

79
00:04:12,297 --> 00:04:13,587
Okay.

80
00:04:14,238 --> 00:04:15,463
I came to check on him.

81
00:04:15,465 --> 00:04:17,247
I felt bad calling you all the time.

82
00:04:17,888 --> 00:04:18,905
Right.

83
00:04:19,152 --> 00:04:21,945
I should treat you to a meal...

84
00:04:21,978 --> 00:04:23,905
No, I know you're busy.

85
00:04:23,907 --> 00:04:26,460
And I only stepped out
during my lunch break.

86
00:04:26,937 --> 00:04:27,937
Then I'll go.

87
00:04:32,623 --> 00:04:34,561
- You don't have to walk me out.
- It's fine.

88
00:04:34,659 --> 00:04:37,783
- I should walk a little when I have time.
- Okay.

89
00:04:37,844 --> 00:04:38,846
What about your mother?

90
00:04:39,027 --> 00:04:41,344
She's coming back tonight.
I guess work went well.

91
00:04:41,434 --> 00:04:42,516
That's a relief.

92
00:04:43,565 --> 00:04:46,358
When O Reum grows up,
I'll make sure to tell him.

93
00:04:46,598 --> 00:04:49,405
He should know who his lifesaver is.

94
00:04:50,206 --> 00:04:52,288
I don't expect anything like that.

95
00:05:07,752 --> 00:05:08,763
Hello.

96
00:05:10,036 --> 00:05:11,430
Hello.

97
00:05:11,945 --> 00:05:12,953
What...

98
00:05:13,720 --> 00:05:15,700
were you two talking about?

99
00:05:16,045 --> 00:05:18,741
What do you mean, O Reum's lifesaver?

100
00:05:18,889 --> 00:05:20,356
Well...

101
00:05:22,411 --> 00:05:23,411
It's...

102
00:05:24,132 --> 00:05:25,138
Why are you...

103
00:05:25,459 --> 00:05:27,416
talking about O Reum with the doctor?

104
00:05:33,038 --> 00:05:35,021
Please come to my office for a moment.

105
00:05:35,078 --> 00:05:36,083
Doctor,

106
00:05:36,830 --> 00:05:39,108
- I'd like to tell her myself.
- Would you?

107
00:05:39,538 --> 00:05:40,873
Then let's talk in my office.

108
00:05:41,112 --> 00:05:42,627
I'll explain the background first.

109
00:05:43,185 --> 00:05:44,251
Okay.

110
00:05:45,059 --> 00:05:46,065
Let's go.

111
00:05:59,258 --> 00:06:02,101
The person you're calling
is unavailable...

112
00:06:02,109 --> 00:06:03,117
She's not answering.

113
00:06:04,045 --> 00:06:05,994
She must've fallen asleep
making lunchboxes.

114
00:06:06,499 --> 00:06:07,602
Yeong Ju...

115
00:06:07,774 --> 00:06:09,083
must've been tired lately.

116
00:06:13,092 --> 00:06:14,101
But, Seung Hyun,

117
00:06:14,289 --> 00:06:17,092
I think O Reum has put on some weight.

118
00:06:17,118 --> 00:06:18,305
Am I the only one who thinks so?

119
00:06:18,398 --> 00:06:20,657
I said that this morning and got scolded.

120
00:06:21,311 --> 00:06:22,792
I guess we just want to see it.

121
00:06:23,300 --> 00:06:27,338
No, I'm telling you,
O Reum's face looks fuller.

122
00:06:27,392 --> 00:06:29,965
The more I look, the more I think so.

123
00:06:30,612 --> 00:06:32,911
Should we just say it does?

124
00:06:33,165 --> 00:06:34,178
Should we?

125
00:06:35,932 --> 00:06:39,484
- You're such a fool, Seung Hyun.
- You're even more of a fool.

126
00:06:41,045 --> 00:06:42,886
- O Reum.
- Our precious O Reum.

127
00:06:47,431 --> 00:06:50,563
I'm so shocked and confused.

128
00:06:52,578 --> 00:06:54,627
I don't know what to say.

129
00:06:55,945 --> 00:06:58,517
I'm the one who's sorry for deceiving you.

130
00:06:59,172 --> 00:07:01,338
Even while watching you suffer,

131
00:07:01,583 --> 00:07:03,671
I couldn't say anything.

132
00:07:05,298 --> 00:07:06,311
Right.

133
00:07:06,571 --> 00:07:08,258
This must stay a secret.

134
00:07:08,752 --> 00:07:11,105
It would be hard on my mom
if she found out.

135
00:07:11,565 --> 00:07:12,588
I...

136
00:07:13,089 --> 00:07:15,775
I've never kept a secret from mom before.

137
00:07:16,212 --> 00:07:17,224
Do you...

138
00:07:17,792 --> 00:07:18,988
not resent me?

139
00:07:21,685 --> 00:07:23,655
If I really think back,

140
00:07:23,949 --> 00:07:25,613
I do remember feeling hurt.

141
00:07:26,005 --> 00:07:27,955
I had a lot of anger...

142
00:07:28,267 --> 00:07:29,330
and resentment.

143
00:07:29,945 --> 00:07:32,686
Maybe it's still there deep down.

144
00:07:35,265 --> 00:07:37,517
I don't know.
I haven't thought that deeply.

145
00:07:37,884 --> 00:07:39,450
You're avoiding it.

146
00:07:41,045 --> 00:07:42,590
Why would you force yourself...

147
00:07:43,202 --> 00:07:44,782
to recall such painful memories?

148
00:07:47,152 --> 00:07:50,288
You got close to O Reum
during the funeral, right?

149
00:07:52,805 --> 00:07:54,007
I guess so.

150
00:07:54,785 --> 00:07:55,971
I see.

151
00:07:58,085 --> 00:07:59,925
Blood really does bind people together.

152
00:08:01,938 --> 00:08:03,534
No matter how hard I tried to erase it,

153
00:08:05,064 --> 00:08:07,465
blood ties are really powerful.

154
00:08:07,467 --> 00:08:09,898
Honestly, I never thought of it that way.

155
00:08:10,552 --> 00:08:12,232
If I had something...

156
00:08:12,580 --> 00:08:14,311
that could save O Reum,

157
00:08:15,267 --> 00:08:16,575
I thought I should give it.

158
00:08:16,873 --> 00:08:18,067
It was that simple.

159
00:08:20,532 --> 00:08:21,688
My mom...

160
00:08:21,770 --> 00:08:23,740
hates how simple I am.

161
00:08:24,158 --> 00:08:25,373
I can understand that.

162
00:08:26,892 --> 00:08:28,713
My mom is different from me.

163
00:08:28,774 --> 00:08:29,782
I know.

164
00:08:29,849 --> 00:08:32,038
I'll keep it a secret.

165
00:08:32,333 --> 00:08:33,351
Don't worry.

166
00:08:34,972 --> 00:08:36,465
You've done so much for us.

167
00:08:37,986 --> 00:08:40,658
I can't put you in a difficult position.

168
00:08:44,925 --> 00:08:45,934
Okay.

169
00:08:47,382 --> 00:08:49,771
I'll pray that the transplant...

170
00:08:50,742 --> 00:08:51,946
engrafts successfully.

171
00:08:54,912 --> 00:08:56,180
Thank you.

172
00:08:57,972 --> 00:08:59,123
I don't even know...

173
00:09:00,587 --> 00:09:03,215
how to thank you enough.

174
00:09:03,889 --> 00:09:04,938
I'm ashamed.

175
00:09:06,058 --> 00:09:07,259
I was more...

176
00:09:08,045 --> 00:09:09,784
of an adult than you.

177
00:09:11,264 --> 00:09:13,617
But I wasn't as mature as you are now.

178
00:09:14,372 --> 00:09:15,884
Even though you did nothing wrong,

179
00:09:16,753 --> 00:09:19,092
I lumped you in with the adults.

180
00:09:21,102 --> 00:09:22,780
I even hated you.

181
00:09:25,145 --> 00:09:28,063
You only see O Reum as O Reum,

182
00:09:29,477 --> 00:09:30,967
and that shames me.

183
00:09:32,814 --> 00:09:34,846
You were directly involved.

184
00:09:35,218 --> 00:09:36,436
My mom...

185
00:09:36,704 --> 00:09:39,813
and you were both part of what happened.
So I understand.

186
00:09:40,638 --> 00:09:41,646
But...

187
00:09:43,067 --> 00:09:44,530
O Reum and I...

188
00:09:47,332 --> 00:09:50,246
were born knowing nothing
about what happened.

189
00:09:51,985 --> 00:09:54,013
That's why I'm comfortable around him.

190
00:09:58,585 --> 00:10:00,702
I just stepped out during lunch.

191
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:03,532
Okay. Get back.

192
00:10:09,225 --> 00:10:10,430
I'm sorry...

193
00:10:11,225 --> 00:10:12,292
and thank you.

194
00:10:46,971 --> 00:10:47,974
Please.

195
00:10:47,976 --> 00:10:50,463
Ma'am, please let me
become Cha Ji Ni.

196
00:10:50,537 --> 00:10:52,240
Please. Okay?

197
00:10:54,038 --> 00:10:55,125
Dad,

198
00:10:56,124 --> 00:10:57,692
I don't want to think about it.

199
00:10:58,238 --> 00:10:59,834
I don't want to remember.

200
00:11:00,985 --> 00:11:02,223
I just...

201
00:11:03,205 --> 00:11:04,871
want to live as Na Ji Ni.

202
00:11:19,198 --> 00:11:20,698
Yeong Ju!

203
00:11:21,294 --> 00:11:22,415
Mrs. No!

204
00:11:23,663 --> 00:11:24,664
What?

205
00:11:25,032 --> 00:11:28,019
What are you thinking about?
You didn't even hear me calling you.

206
00:11:28,632 --> 00:11:30,114
I'm starving.

207
00:11:30,116 --> 00:11:32,055
I was about to collapse waiting for lunch.

208
00:11:33,281 --> 00:11:34,450
How's O Reum?

209
00:11:34,517 --> 00:11:35,518
He's doing great.

210
00:11:35,618 --> 00:11:39,298
He's starting to look
more and more like his old self.

211
00:11:39,694 --> 00:11:40,698
Really?

212
00:11:42,132 --> 00:11:44,530
Your cooking skills have improved again.

213
00:12:06,172 --> 00:12:07,290
O Reum,

214
00:12:07,796 --> 00:12:09,432
you know the drawing lady, right?

215
00:12:10,445 --> 00:12:12,567
She saved your life.

216
00:12:13,785 --> 00:12:15,044
That lady...

217
00:12:15,924 --> 00:12:17,632
is your aunt, O Reum.

218
00:12:18,438 --> 00:12:20,546
The aunt I hated.

219
00:12:25,345 --> 00:12:26,638
How could I ever...

220
00:12:27,779 --> 00:12:29,321
repay her for this?

221
00:12:32,998 --> 00:12:34,221
Here.

222
00:12:34,374 --> 00:12:35,848
Here.

223
00:12:39,332 --> 00:12:41,802
Ma'am, is this all you have? Just ties?

224
00:12:41,805 --> 00:12:44,908
I used to buy clothes
when I traveled for performances.

225
00:12:44,969 --> 00:12:46,361
But now I'm a businesswoman.

226
00:12:47,051 --> 00:12:48,255
This is boring.

227
00:12:48,465 --> 00:12:49,478
Did...

228
00:12:49,659 --> 00:12:52,272
- you do what I asked?
- Of course.

229
00:12:52,533 --> 00:12:54,783
I kept a close eye on her
around the clock.

230
00:12:54,785 --> 00:12:56,333
She never even went near the hospital.

231
00:12:57,054 --> 00:12:58,065
Good.

232
00:12:58,798 --> 00:13:00,380
I can hear everything.

233
00:13:04,585 --> 00:13:05,604
Here.

234
00:13:06,905 --> 00:13:09,265
Did everything work out?

235
00:13:10,154 --> 00:13:11,657
Of course.

236
00:13:12,132 --> 00:13:15,738
Seeing it in person, it was huge.

237
00:13:15,951 --> 00:13:19,242
I walked around with the attorney,
and my jaw just dropped.

238
00:13:19,454 --> 00:13:21,194
You should thank dad.

239
00:13:22,030 --> 00:13:23,110
That's a relief.

240
00:13:23,112 --> 00:13:26,336
Those people from that family
didn't come anywhere near you, right?

241
00:13:29,232 --> 00:13:32,575
- They came again?
- Not exactly. They found a donor.

242
00:13:32,811 --> 00:13:35,073
- I heard the transplant is happening now.
- Really?

243
00:13:36,368 --> 00:13:37,636
Where did they find one?

244
00:13:37,638 --> 00:13:39,851
There are good people in this world.

245
00:13:41,005 --> 00:13:42,765
Anyway, that's a relief.

246
00:13:43,726 --> 00:13:44,758
Right?

247
00:13:45,212 --> 00:13:47,305
I said the same thing when I heard.

248
00:13:47,505 --> 00:13:49,948
If you didn't help him
and then heard he passed away,

249
00:13:49,979 --> 00:13:52,332
- it would've felt awful.
- Exactly.

250
00:13:52,438 --> 00:13:53,486
So...

251
00:13:53,602 --> 00:13:55,737
don't say things like
you're keeping a close eye on me.

252
00:13:55,739 --> 00:13:57,048
Don't worry about me.

253
00:13:57,192 --> 00:13:58,565
We're busy with work.

254
00:13:58,815 --> 00:14:00,011
Let's just focus on our own things.

255
00:14:00,013 --> 00:14:02,140
That's exactly how I feel.

256
00:14:02,247 --> 00:14:03,272
Jung A.

257
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:13,284
That's a relief.

258
00:14:18,645 --> 00:14:20,455
Your grandson survived.

259
00:14:20,786 --> 00:14:21,938
That's good.

260
00:14:24,407 --> 00:14:25,690
I'm glad it worked out.

261
00:14:26,811 --> 00:14:28,702
I just didn't want to get involved,

262
00:14:28,704 --> 00:14:30,777
but I never wished
for things to get worse.

263
00:14:33,220 --> 00:14:35,067
- Welcome.
- Hello.

264
00:14:36,074 --> 00:14:37,830
One iced Americano, please.

265
00:14:37,876 --> 00:14:40,350
- Sure. I'll ring you up.
- Thanks.

266
00:14:41,772 --> 00:14:44,232
- You're the singing class teacher, right?
- Yes. Have you seen me before?

267
00:14:44,285 --> 00:14:46,438
You've come here
with your students a few times.

268
00:14:48,083 --> 00:14:49,873
- Please wait a moment.
- Sure.

269
00:14:57,850 --> 00:15:00,873
Did you negotiate the rent? What happened?

270
00:15:01,064 --> 00:15:02,650
They did tell me it was going up.

271
00:15:02,714 --> 00:15:05,000
But they haven't contacted me again,
so I'm still waiting.

272
00:15:05,106 --> 00:15:06,694
- Is it the same here?
- Yes.

273
00:15:07,032 --> 00:15:10,836
Waiting anxiously with no news
is even scarier, right?

274
00:15:10,856 --> 00:15:12,675
Exactly. I'm the same.

275
00:15:15,114 --> 00:15:18,225
Every time I come here,
I love the interior.

276
00:15:19,212 --> 00:15:21,677
I studied fine arts, you know.

277
00:15:21,885 --> 00:15:24,420
I see. I hope you sell a lot today.

278
00:15:24,483 --> 00:15:28,157
- Thank you. Have a nice day.
- You too.

279
00:15:41,843 --> 00:15:44,109
What? You seem to be in a good mood.

280
00:15:44,112 --> 00:15:45,575
Is it because of O Reum?

281
00:15:46,150 --> 00:15:47,207
Of course.

282
00:15:47,290 --> 00:15:50,229
I think this is what they mean
by being full without eating.

283
00:15:50,232 --> 00:15:53,032
He's adjusting well, right?

284
00:15:54,103 --> 00:15:55,598
Even though they're not family,

285
00:15:55,666 --> 00:15:57,831
the fact that someone in this world
is a bone marrow match...

286
00:15:57,833 --> 00:15:59,570
is nothing short of a miracle.

287
00:15:59,573 --> 00:16:02,577
I still can't believe
that person was actually found.

288
00:16:02,584 --> 00:16:03,729
I know.

289
00:16:04,314 --> 00:16:06,083
Even from both sides of the family,

290
00:16:06,085 --> 00:16:09,317
not a single person was a match.

291
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:12,683
You really never know
what life has in store.

292
00:16:12,685 --> 00:16:13,934
Exactly.

293
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:16,289
Want to see something interesting?

294
00:16:20,952 --> 00:16:22,169
This.

295
00:16:23,321 --> 00:16:25,205
- My goodness.
- This...

296
00:16:25,669 --> 00:16:26,900
Look!

297
00:16:27,850 --> 00:16:29,971
I wanted to keep it without washing it,

298
00:16:30,083 --> 00:16:31,690
but I had no choice
but to wash it and wear it.

299
00:16:32,613 --> 00:16:33,948
My goodness, erase it quickly.

300
00:16:33,950 --> 00:16:35,982
Why would you keep something like this?
It's ugly.

301
00:16:36,310 --> 00:16:37,561
No.

302
00:16:38,921 --> 00:16:39,989
No way.

303
00:16:39,991 --> 00:16:42,642
When O Reum gets much older,
I'm going to show him this photo.

304
00:16:43,100 --> 00:16:46,010
And tell him,
"You were in so much pain back then...

305
00:16:46,100 --> 00:16:48,412
you could've bathed in your grandma's
and your parents' tears."

306
00:16:48,414 --> 00:16:50,862
That's right. There'd still be enough left
after a bath.

307
00:16:50,908 --> 00:16:52,717
His mom is still crying.

308
00:16:53,712 --> 00:16:56,472
Anyway, erase it quickly.
It looks terrible.

309
00:16:56,530 --> 00:16:58,871
I'll buy you ten T-shirts.

310
00:16:59,817 --> 00:17:03,711
Then please keep it under ten dollars.

311
00:17:04,062 --> 00:17:07,863
Or you can just repay me later
over chicken and beer.

312
00:17:08,521 --> 00:17:10,115
Sure, I'll do that.

313
00:17:10,942 --> 00:17:13,644
Hello. You're early today.

314
00:17:15,628 --> 00:17:18,088
Mrs. No, are you raising our tuition?

315
00:17:18,878 --> 00:17:22,356
I think I might have to. How did you know?

316
00:17:22,450 --> 00:17:25,177
Everyone in this building
is sighing these days.

317
00:17:25,272 --> 00:17:28,059
I'm thinking of either
raising the tuition...

318
00:17:28,062 --> 00:17:31,661
or putting the singing class
on hold for a while.

319
00:17:31,961 --> 00:17:34,020
Why? The rent...

320
00:17:34,074 --> 00:17:37,167
That's part of it,
but when O Reum gets discharged,

321
00:17:37,329 --> 00:17:40,371
I'm not sure he'll be able
to start daycare right away,

322
00:17:40,390 --> 00:17:43,088
and it'll be too much for Mai alone.

323
00:17:43,382 --> 00:17:46,982
I feel like I need to be home.

324
00:17:47,859 --> 00:17:50,825
But you said this singing time
was your way of breathing.

325
00:17:51,190 --> 00:17:53,540
I still haven't decided.

326
00:17:53,544 --> 00:17:56,977
Don't worry about the rent.
Take your time deciding.

327
00:17:58,975 --> 00:18:00,163
Sir,

328
00:18:00,723 --> 00:18:02,950
A refund request came in
for the paintings we sold.

329
00:18:04,457 --> 00:18:07,167
- I know.
- Do you know the buyer?

330
00:18:07,332 --> 00:18:09,775
Yes, it's someone I know a little.

331
00:18:11,097 --> 00:18:13,267
- No, actually, it was me.
- Sorry?

332
00:18:13,704 --> 00:18:15,729
You bought them
and now you're returning them?

333
00:18:15,732 --> 00:18:17,086
Not exactly.

334
00:18:19,371 --> 00:18:20,712
Because of my position,

335
00:18:20,714 --> 00:18:22,754
my parents must have bought them
without telling me.

336
00:18:23,177 --> 00:18:24,773
I told them it's fine and to cancel it.

337
00:18:26,491 --> 00:18:27,763
This is a bit embarrassing.

338
00:18:28,634 --> 00:18:30,236
Please keep this
between the two of you.

339
00:18:30,912 --> 00:18:34,027
I can't pretend I don't know anything
even in front of you.

340
00:18:34,331 --> 00:18:35,838
Understood.

341
00:19:05,270 --> 00:19:06,832
- She says she doesn't want to see you.
- What about the paintings?

342
00:19:06,912 --> 00:19:08,632
Workers took them away this morning.

343
00:19:08,652 --> 00:19:11,109
What on earth happened?
Did you confront her?

344
00:19:11,112 --> 00:19:13,046
Did you talk back and mess up?

345
00:19:14,650 --> 00:19:16,904
- I hit Ji Hu.
- In front of her?

346
00:19:16,967 --> 00:19:17,967
Yes.

347
00:19:18,512 --> 00:19:20,919
She doesn't even realize
her son's a petty jerk.

348
00:19:21,192 --> 00:19:22,698
If I were her,
I'd be comforting me, not him.

349
00:19:22,714 --> 00:19:25,500
Honestly, none of them are very bright.

350
00:19:25,973 --> 00:19:27,856
Watch your mouth. What if she comes out?

351
00:19:27,923 --> 00:19:30,009
You think I'm not just as angry?

352
00:19:30,132 --> 00:19:32,186
I'm pissed too right now.

353
00:19:33,492 --> 00:19:34,752
I'll come back later.

354
00:19:41,123 --> 00:19:43,485
No wonder she doesn't want to see you.

355
00:19:44,478 --> 00:19:47,096
Mr. Landlord, please help yourself.

356
00:19:47,712 --> 00:19:49,877
Thanks to you, I feel like
I've gained ten extra years of life.

357
00:19:49,986 --> 00:19:51,942
Thank you. Seriously.

358
00:19:52,794 --> 00:19:55,527
You didn't know? I did.

359
00:19:55,830 --> 00:19:59,418
I kept quiet for the sake of...

360
00:19:59,522 --> 00:20:02,522
- adding some tension to your life.
- That's still too much.

361
00:20:02,575 --> 00:20:04,980
You saw how worried
she was the whole time.

362
00:20:05,072 --> 00:20:06,661
I told him not to say anything.

363
00:20:06,866 --> 00:20:08,542
It won't do any good
if you know he's my uncle.

364
00:20:08,689 --> 00:20:09,876
Why not?

365
00:20:10,030 --> 00:20:12,386
You thought I'd cling to you? Be annoying?

366
00:20:12,596 --> 00:20:13,794
Yes.

367
00:20:15,771 --> 00:20:17,127
Fair point.

368
00:20:18,192 --> 00:20:20,143
Still, that was excessive.

369
00:20:20,146 --> 00:20:21,663
Jung A, that's enough.

370
00:20:21,670 --> 00:20:23,169
You're in full court-lady mode.
You're being too servile.

371
00:20:23,262 --> 00:20:25,767
That's my default setting.
Didn't you know?

372
00:20:31,632 --> 00:20:34,832
- Do Hee.
- You drag me through the mud and laugh?

373
00:20:35,358 --> 00:20:36,558
Let's go.

374
00:20:42,312 --> 00:20:45,242
- I'll see you next time, Uncle.
- Yeah.

375
00:20:45,961 --> 00:20:47,314
I'm heading out. See you later.

376
00:20:47,316 --> 00:20:48,316
See you later.

377
00:20:52,020 --> 00:20:54,271
Even the director can't stand up to her.

378
00:20:54,845 --> 00:20:56,084
But Uncle,

379
00:20:56,554 --> 00:20:58,723
haven't you been living
a little too safely?

380
00:20:59,081 --> 00:21:02,590
Maybe it's time for a risky relationship,
something with a little thrill.

381
00:21:03,490 --> 00:21:05,941
So, what's our landlord's type?

382
00:21:05,944 --> 00:21:08,527
I've got an aunt on my mom's side
and one on my dad's side too.

383
00:21:08,992 --> 00:21:10,944
Lunch break's almost over,
aren't you moving?

384
00:21:11,890 --> 00:21:13,267
Thanks for the ice cream.

385
00:21:13,270 --> 00:21:16,240
When the rent goes up next time,
I'll come back for another treat. I'm off.

386
00:21:16,647 --> 00:21:17,669
Rent...

387
00:21:18,946 --> 00:21:21,161
He's got his guard up tight.

388
00:21:22,373 --> 00:21:24,307
- Shall we go too?
- Yeah.

389
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:27,670
You said you're teaching kids
this afternoon, right?

390
00:21:28,323 --> 00:21:30,066
First step toward becoming rich.

391
00:21:30,137 --> 00:21:33,128
I'm just doing a side job
making books at kids' level.

392
00:21:33,131 --> 00:21:35,782
That's reassuring. I'm rooting for you.

393
00:21:36,312 --> 00:21:38,682
So that means
I should let you off early today, right?

394
00:21:38,685 --> 00:21:39,851
- Yes.
- Yes.

395
00:21:39,931 --> 00:21:41,252
Okay, dismissed.

396
00:21:48,710 --> 00:21:50,113
I'm home.

397
00:21:53,784 --> 00:21:56,313
What's this? Soybean noodles?

398
00:21:58,083 --> 00:21:59,357
For your son?

399
00:21:59,994 --> 00:22:02,470
As if I'd give it
to my unemployed son. Dream on.

400
00:22:02,950 --> 00:22:04,487
It's for my daughter-in-law.

401
00:22:04,672 --> 00:22:06,420
Mai's been really worn out lately.

402
00:22:06,972 --> 00:22:10,336
- Soybeans are the best protein in summer.
- What about your son?

403
00:22:11,198 --> 00:22:12,727
He can eat or not, I don't care.

404
00:22:13,930 --> 00:22:15,459
How does love change like this?

405
00:22:17,172 --> 00:22:18,502
How did the interview go?

406
00:22:18,732 --> 00:22:20,412
You said you'd get a job within ten days.

407
00:22:20,542 --> 00:22:22,102
Can you extend it to a month?

408
00:22:23,401 --> 00:22:25,400
They need time to discuss things.

409
00:22:25,450 --> 00:22:27,405
Who decides on the spot after one meeting?

410
00:22:27,451 --> 00:22:29,386
Then why'd you lie and say ten days?

411
00:22:31,653 --> 00:22:32,866
Try the broth.

412
00:22:37,127 --> 00:22:39,480
Super rich. This is amazing.

413
00:22:44,163 --> 00:22:47,763
I wanted to buy you more,
but I didn't have time to shop.

414
00:22:47,927 --> 00:22:50,292
So this is all I got
at the duty-free shop, sorry.

415
00:22:51,220 --> 00:22:52,220
You didn't have to.

416
00:22:52,584 --> 00:22:53,944
I'm so honored.

417
00:22:55,514 --> 00:22:58,840
Compared to what I've received from you,
this is nothing.

418
00:23:00,012 --> 00:23:01,548
Thank you, I'll cherish it.

419
00:23:02,369 --> 00:23:04,898
- By the way, you look tan.
- Right?

420
00:23:05,410 --> 00:23:08,344
Indonesia was amazing.

421
00:23:08,740 --> 00:23:13,257
When I used to travel for performances,
I only saw concert halls and city centers,

422
00:23:13,295 --> 00:23:16,123
but this time I actually got to explore.

423
00:23:16,572 --> 00:23:18,682
You should go sometime.

424
00:23:18,933 --> 00:23:21,657
- For a honeymoon?
- That would be perfect.

425
00:23:22,690 --> 00:23:24,348
So do you have someone now?

426
00:23:24,432 --> 00:23:27,132
- In just one week without me?
- I'm kidding.

427
00:23:27,850 --> 00:23:29,746
But why did you cut your trip short?

428
00:23:29,809 --> 00:23:31,930
Didn't you say
you had lots of parties scheduled?

429
00:23:32,390 --> 00:23:33,796
Because of my daughter.

430
00:23:34,384 --> 00:23:38,290
She's not staying with her dad.
I felt bad leaving her, so I came back.

431
00:23:39,790 --> 00:23:42,675
I guess that's why they say it's hard
to raise a child alone.

432
00:23:43,800 --> 00:23:45,129
Have you improved on the cello?

433
00:23:45,132 --> 00:23:47,330
Did you memorize the finger positions?

434
00:23:47,780 --> 00:23:50,565
Yes. Memorizing isn't that hard,

435
00:23:51,085 --> 00:23:54,075
but I'm not sure if the pitch
I'm producing is correct.

436
00:23:54,132 --> 00:23:56,642
As I said, I'm tone-deaf.

437
00:23:57,118 --> 00:23:58,118
Want to try?

438
00:23:58,904 --> 00:23:59,969
Now?

439
00:24:01,064 --> 00:24:02,184
Here.

440
00:24:06,175 --> 00:24:07,544
Good.

441
00:24:08,723 --> 00:24:09,918
Use a bit more strength.

442
00:24:09,969 --> 00:24:11,596
You need to apply pressure here.

443
00:24:14,419 --> 00:24:17,788
Let me guide you. Try bowing. Again.

444
00:24:26,078 --> 00:24:28,690
A bit more pressure. Good.

445
00:24:29,817 --> 00:24:31,994
You've improved a lot.

446
00:24:32,083 --> 00:24:35,419
With repetition, your ears will start
to recognize the sound too.

447
00:24:36,125 --> 00:24:39,370
Singing depends on your body,
so pitch can be off,

448
00:24:39,432 --> 00:24:44,238
but with an instrument, proper finger
position and bowing produce a true sound.

449
00:24:46,155 --> 00:24:47,669
The sheet music matters,

450
00:24:47,847 --> 00:24:50,252
but when you play, in that moment,

451
00:24:50,254 --> 00:24:53,723
try thinking, "I am the music."

452
00:24:53,890 --> 00:24:57,944
At that moment,
it's just you and the cello.

453
00:24:58,626 --> 00:24:59,626
Yes.

454
00:25:00,660 --> 00:25:04,146
That one-minute lesson
completely changed my mindset.

455
00:25:05,592 --> 00:25:07,165
It's different from just watching, right?

456
00:25:07,396 --> 00:25:09,307
Yes. I'm moved.

457
00:25:25,687 --> 00:25:26,687
Hey.

458
00:25:38,412 --> 00:25:39,800
What brings you here?

459
00:25:39,973 --> 00:25:42,592
This is good for you
in the summer. Drink it.

460
00:25:44,596 --> 00:25:46,354
You didn't have to do this.

461
00:25:46,356 --> 00:25:48,246
It's just a gesture. It's nothing.

462
00:25:49,190 --> 00:25:50,638
Just accept it as a gesture from me.

463
00:26:14,078 --> 00:26:15,846
Mix it with a bit of water
when you drink it.

464
00:26:16,361 --> 00:26:18,396
O Reum really likes this too.

465
00:26:18,792 --> 00:26:21,465
I hope...

466
00:26:21,969 --> 00:26:24,825
you can share it with him someday.

467
00:26:26,500 --> 00:26:29,184
Yes. Thank you. I'll enjoy it.

468
00:26:56,919 --> 00:26:58,024
What?

469
00:26:59,460 --> 00:27:01,167
It was really delicious.

470
00:27:01,692 --> 00:27:06,082
I hope I can share it
with O Reum someday too.

471
00:27:12,617 --> 00:27:14,572
How is it? Good, right?

472
00:27:15,043 --> 00:27:16,382
Pho is nice too,

473
00:27:16,384 --> 00:27:20,437
but your husband and O Reum like this,
so you should get used to it as well.

474
00:27:22,090 --> 00:27:23,782
I miss cilantro.

475
00:27:23,876 --> 00:27:26,832
I forgot to stop by the store,
just eat it as is.

476
00:27:34,453 --> 00:27:36,085
What's Ji Ni talking about?

477
00:27:36,912 --> 00:27:38,999
What?

478
00:27:39,001 --> 00:27:42,247
Did you bring soybean noodles
to Ji Ni too?

479
00:27:42,756 --> 00:27:43,944
Why?

480
00:27:45,497 --> 00:27:47,887
Why are you looking at my phone?

481
00:27:48,933 --> 00:27:50,154
Mom.

482
00:28:14,774 --> 00:28:17,919
(Family Register)

483
00:28:17,994 --> 00:28:19,830
This must stay absolutely secret.

484
00:28:19,881 --> 00:28:21,927
- I owe her a huge debt.
- This is serious.

485
00:28:21,982 --> 00:28:23,796
Secrets keep getting out.
I'm getting nervous.

486
00:28:23,838 --> 00:28:25,885
Does Ji Ni have some kind of secret too?

487
00:28:25,944 --> 00:28:27,144
Why don't you date, Ji Ni?

488
00:28:27,194 --> 00:28:28,472
I hate relationships like my dad's...

489
00:28:28,474 --> 00:28:30,670
and relationships like my mom's.

490
00:28:30,740 --> 00:28:33,961
I just hope this doesn't cause problems
for the girl.

491
00:28:34,007 --> 00:28:36,693
Let's stop. I'm so sick of this.

492
00:28:38,428 --> 00:28:40,731
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
